  "review_conclusions": [
    "ProjectTemplateId selects a closed built-in registry. Descriptor deserialization compares all persisted metadata and entry descriptors against the canonical registry before returning its lightweight ID handle;independent leaf metadata is not file authenticity.",
    "Template source SHA-256 sorts embedded path/payload records with a domain label and length prefixes. The digest identifies the original embedded pack before name/GUID or optional engine-range rewriting;rendered project bytes have a different identity.",
    "Rendering validates portable names,lexical relative paths,duplicates,file-as-ancestor conflicts and required provider selections,then returns owned entries and summary. This layer neither confines a physical output root nor writes files,loads providers or activates a project.",
    "Manifest rewriting decodes and reencodes structured TOML,so it preserves intended fields and semantics rather than original formatting bytes. Source payload digest stays attached to the source descriptor.",
    "Provenance binds caller-supplied operation,engine and BuildSet values. Receipt construction/deserialization validates schema,canonical descriptor and engine compatibility;it does not authenticate launch admission or prove that filesystem creation happened.",
    "Ordinary Editor draft creation renders before transaction writes. The preflighted adapter reuses the rendered value produced earlier. Receipt issuance precedes filesystem write/preflight/commit;physical ownership and cleanup remain the creation transaction's responsibility.",
    "All23 tests are static/serde/fixture evidence. Scene and asset TOML assertions do not execute Runtime decoding,rendering,provider loading or activation. The new68/31 supplement supplies real source ranges while preserving the original malformed record and explicit corrections."
  ],
